WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.569
-My first guest tonight
is an Oscar-winning actress.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:08.174
She stars in the new movie "F9,"
which is in theaters today.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.543
Here is Charlize Theron.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.844
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.813
-Oh, my goodness, come on, now!

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.582
Oh! We love you.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.284
Charlize.
-Hi, Jimmy.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.219
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.755
I appreciate this
every time you come.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.658
Congrats on "F9."

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.293
I think this --
I mean, obviously I think

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.728
it's going to be
the biggest movie.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.731
I think this is the movie that's
going to open up movies again.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.699
Everyone's gonna go
to the theater this weekend

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:34.934
and check it out.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.971
Congrats on being in this.
This is your second one.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.205
-Thank you.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.373
Thank you for having --

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.241
Thank you for saying
all those kind words.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:46.178
And yes, I -- Have you missed
movies, going to the theater?

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:47.179
'Cause I have.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.447
-Yes, of course I have.
-So much.

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:51.017
-Especially with this movie,
which is --

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.886
You take it to a new level
in this "Fast and Furious."

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:55.855
Actually, you go to space in --

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.890
That's not a spoiler.
It's out there.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.593
But here's what I love.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.061
You play Cipher.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.664
And you're a villain
in the movie,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.966
and your hair choice,
I will say, is fantastic.

00:01:07.966 --> 00:01:10.002
You chose a bowl cut.

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:12.972
And you still look cool.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:13.973
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.274
You are just so cool-looking

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:17.143
that you look awesome
with a bowl cut.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.445
Look at this.
I love that.

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:22.648
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:24.751
How do you pull that off?

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.286
-I don't know if I did,

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.455
but thank you
for selling it so hard.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.124
-[ Laughing ] You did.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.860
-You know what?
I was working on a movie

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.196
and I had shorter hair,

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:40.266
and I went right into the shoot
after I wrapped that film.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.668
And I just -- I didn't have
that much hair to work with,

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:45.672
and we didn't have enough time
to build a wig,

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:48.741
so we just didn't have
that much choice.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:52.044
And the only thing that
we really could do was that.

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:54.647
And thank God
I have so much trust

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.315
in the people that I work with.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:59.319
-I pulled a similar look
when I was a child.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.821
That was me here.
That was --

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.256
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:06.659
We look like we could be
brother and sister, kind of.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:10.229
-I mean, I think every kid
had, like, a bowl cut, right?

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.197
Like, I had one, too.

00:02:12.197 --> 00:02:14.400
-Yeah, I asked you for a picture
of you with a bowl cut,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.836
and, oh, my goodness,
this is what you sent us.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.171
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.773
-Oh, my goodness.
Stop!

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.443
Are you kidding me?
How cute is this baby?

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.913
Oh, my gosh.
You were so cute.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.247
-Aww.

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:29.748
-It's the tiniest little
bowl cut.

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:31.450
It's like a little --

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.653
-Yet again, I didn't have
that much hair to work with.

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:36.155
[ Laughs ]

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.991
-Cipher's name is an alias.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:41.594
You've used aliases probably
before in real life,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.061
like if you stay at a hotel.

00:02:43.061 --> 00:02:44.196
Do you ever stay under --

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:45.899
You don't stay
under your name, do you?

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.299
You change it up?
-I do.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:52.505
I had one that people were
really kind of weirded out by,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.406
which really came from
a very innocent place

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.942
because I took it
off a cereal box --

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:58.211
Ginger Raspberry --

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.246
but everybody thought
it was very stripper-like.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.413
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:04.516
-Yeah, Ginger Raspberry.
-I know.

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:06.585
-Coming to the stage,
put your hands together

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:08.454
for Ginger Raspberry.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.389
[ Airhorn honks ]

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:12.892
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.827
Yeah, yeah.
Ginger Raspberry.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.795
No, you can't do that.

00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:19.132
It almost takes
more explaining than --

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.099
just put my own name down there.

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:23.402
-I just felt like room service
never took me serious.

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:25.470
-[ Laughs ] Ginger Raspberry.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.040
I want to talk about "F9"

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.842
because you know I love
your acting.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.244
But this acting
is a good challenge.

00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:35.314
You act most of the movie
in a box.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:37.383
You're in a Plexiglas box.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.653
-I am. I do well
when I'm given boundaries.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.688
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.391
-Yeah.
-Listen, I definitely think

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.760
some actors really like to have
a lot of freedom

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.429
and to use space
and things like that.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:52.832
I tend to -- I have learned
over the years

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.100
that it's maybe better for me
to just have boundaries

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.203
and have somebody say,
"This is where you are,

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.072
and you're working with this."

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:03.109
Because I remember
when I had to audition,

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.544
when I was starting out,
and going --

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:07.746
First of all, I didn't know
what an audition was,

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.016
so I didn't even really know
how to prepare for it.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.918
But the idea of walking into

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:15.554
an office building room
with fluorescent lights

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.390
and not having boundaries,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.992
not having somebody say,
"This is where you are,

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:24.530
this is what you do,"
I -- I don't take well to it.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.934
I have memories
of doing the craziest things,

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.771
like bringing in ketchup

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:36.409
and, like, squirting ketchup all
over the floor and on myself,

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:40.212
because I was auditioning for a
scene where I was getting shot.

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:42.281
And again, I just needed
a director to say,

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:45.050
"You don't need to do that.
You don't need to do that."

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:49.155
-Wait, so they go --
"Next up, Charlize.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.757
Charlize Theron,
can you come in?"

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:53.493
And you would enter
already bloody, or no?

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.327
-Yes, I would do it
in the hallway.

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:56.829
I would kind of
tell the secretary

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.363
I'm going to get loud
for a second,

00:04:58.363 --> 00:04:59.765
cause she's on the phone.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.400
I was trying to be respectful,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.970
and then I would squirt it
all over myself,

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.706
and then I just barge
into the door,

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.274
pretending like I was shot.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:12.545
And I would smear ketchup
on the walls, everywhere.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:16.215
Again, I need somebody to tell
me, "You can't do that.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:19.485
Stay here and just
stand right here."

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:24.390
-There's rumors of an all-female
"Fast" spin-off.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.625
Have you heard that,
and would you be up for it?

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:31.397
-I have been hearing that,
and I don't know anything,

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.631
but yes.

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.766
I mean, I think --
the thing that I will say

00:05:34.766 --> 00:05:38.537
that I think is very impressive
about this franchise

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.406
would be the female characters.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:44.510
I think the women
in this franchise are --

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.412
it's probably
one of the biggest reasons

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.447
why I wanted to be a part of it.

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:50.817
You know, no offense
to Vin Diesel,

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:53.853
but Michelle Rodriguez
is pretty badass.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.788
-Never offense to the Diesel,
yeah.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.790
-And so I think it's a great
idea, and I hope they do it.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:02.361
If they need a baddie with
a bowl cut, I'm available.

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:03.863
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.698
-"F9" is in theaters today.

